Type Plumlang and press Enter: each entry runs at once, and what it declares
stays for the entries after it. An entry that is one expression prints its
value and type. An entry goes on to the next line while a bracket is open or
a line ends with an operator, ',' or '=>'.

Commands:
  :help           this help
  :type <expr>    the type of an expression, without running it
  :load <file>    run a file's code in this session
  :reset          forget everything declared so far
  :quit           leave (also :q, Ctrl-D or exit())

Keys: left/right, Home/End (Ctrl-A/E), Backspace/Delete, up/down for earlier
lines, Ctrl-U/Ctrl-K delete to the start/end, Ctrl-W the word before the
cursor, Ctrl-L clears the screen, Ctrl-C cancels the entry.
